// The ready agents of People & HR (6 Nov 2026): the recurring tasks of an HR business partner, a recruiter, a
// people-operations manager, an L&D lead, a reward analyst and an employee-relations specialist, each done to a senior
// standard. Where an outcome depends on the employment law of a place, the agent sets officialSearch and reads that
// place's official sources; it never invents a statutory period or amount and says when a lawyer or the policy owner
// must confirm.
import { doc, type FieldCatalogue } from './kit.ts';

/** The fairness rule every HR judgement rests on. */
const FAIR = 'Stay lawful, consistent and non-discriminatory: treat like cases alike, never let a protected characteristic (sex, age, race, disability, religion, pregnancy, family status, union membership and the others the place protects) shape a judgement, and record the reasons.';
/** The rule of every agent whose outcome depends on the law of the place. */
const LAW = 'Where the outcome depends on the employment law of the place (notice, statutory periods, pay rules, protected rights, required procedure), read that place\'s official sources and cite them; never state a period, rate or amount you have not read there; where the law or the policy is unclear, say that an employment lawyer or the policy owner must confirm before the step is taken.';

